le="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="86c6ef37-3e44-4617-8f53-0aba2f368ef1" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="97b7baa7-e311-44b5-894f-076db7807c9f"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="124cb895-ee23-4072-b6f8-bf9cf41d134c"><p data-ref="7f94335c-3f0a-4978-a5f1-75229c552d0c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a C program to construct a B-Tree of a given minimum degree. First, insert a list of keys into the B-Tree and print the inorder traversal after all insertions. Then, delete a given set of keys from the B-Tree and again print the inorder traversal. Finally, search for a specific key in the current B-Tree and print whether it is found or not.</p><p data-ref="c0ee234b-2d4e-48e3-8fc1-e13401a05306" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="c6d71538-eed9-45c9-9064-2fea832d4f19"></p><p data-ref="6f548f17-0715-4b09-9bec-9be5beac8ecc" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="d4f1766d-be7f-45fa-b6f5-2df1cbb5fd63">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="b64493de-1a0b-421b-b